WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[Instrumental music.] Scene 1 — Program Cue opens the programme journey.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Three current product views frame the programme’s starting point.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
The message is “From first proposal to published programme.”

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Scene 2 — One workspace maps the programme lifecycle.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Shape, Decide and Share organise the connected steps.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.000
The Command Centre replaces the lifecycle diagram.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Scene 3 — The Command Centre shows event readiness.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Readiness is 75 percent across six workflows.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Two blockers appear in the action queue.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.000
A filtered task list exposes owner and impact.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Scene 4 — Event settings define shared identity and access.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Event data authority is Program Cue or Airtable.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Branding previews appear at desktop and mobile sizes.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.000
A confirmed publish step makes the identity public.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Scene 5 — Five steps govern a versioned application.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Questions include conditional logic and a review purpose.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Desktop and mobile previews remain clearly labelled.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:41.000
Publishing opens stable form version 01 for applications.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:46.000
A verified applicant saves a private draft.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Submission keeps answers with form version 01.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Scene 6 — An evaluator opens the review queue.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:02.000
The workbench combines answers, version and conflict status.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Four weighted scores produce a total of 4.25.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:16.000
Advisory suggestions cite evidence for optional import.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:22.000
The reviewer submits a waitlist recommendation.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Two reviews support a released waitlist decision.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Scene 7 — An accepted session opens speaker preparation.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Desktop and mobile workspaces show the linked session.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:46.000
One onboarding task is complete; two remain open.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.000
The speaker deck completes secure file checks.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:59.000
Event imagery connects speaker preparation to show day.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:06.000
Scene 8 — The Command Centre opens the Event Assistant.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.000
The organiser asks for a draft reminder for approval.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Priya has one incomplete speaker-scoped task.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.000
The reminder template exposes supported merge fields.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:26.000
One speaker-scoped recipient awaits approval.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.000
The reminder enters the queue.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Operation Centre shows approval and queue status.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:39.000
Scene 9 — A speaker welcome opens for review.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:44.000
Alex Morgan’s personalised preview appears.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:50.000
Confirmation rechecks the recipient and template.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:55.000
The delivery status records the welcome handoff result.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Calendar work keeps a separate queue status.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.200
Scene 10 — Conflict-aware scheduling moves towards publication.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:12.000
Two Main Hall sessions overlap at 10:30.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:18.800
Two placements are valid; a third session remains unplaced.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:25.600
Content and speaker checks remain separate.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:32.000
The publication diff preserves the current public programme.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.800
Final confirmation revalidates every dependency.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:40.000
One approved schedule version becomes public.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.000
Scene 11 — Seven views share published programme data.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:50.000
Programme and timetable views appear on two screen sizes.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:55.000
A mobile programme filters to one selected date.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Speaker profiles link people to published sessions.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.000
A personal itinerary holds four saved sessions.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:10.000
A managed embed shows the published programme.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.000
Light, dark and mobile site views appear.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.000
Event imagery brings the programme to life.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.160
Program Cue connects to your stack through 33 documented API paths.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:26.140
The contract explorer shows scoped keys and schemas.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:31.600
Operation recovery follows one reminder to a failed result.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.280
The failed operation keeps its original one-person audience.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:42.000
An Accelevents preview maps one confirmation-ready export.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:47.000
Scene 13 — The product journey resolves into one system.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.000
One programme. Every workflow. Fully connected.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:59.000
The final card shows ProgramCue.com with three product snapshots.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Picture fades.
